WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.350
In this lesson, you will learn to use numbers and repeat blocks to solve puzzles with as few blocks as possible.

2
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:12.530
Some puzzles say “use 3 blocks or fewer”.

3
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.850
Count the blocks in your script.

4
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.950
Right 4 is one block.

5
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.920
Right, right, right, right is four!

6
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.840
If a pattern happens again, put it inside a repeat.

7
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.420
Short code is easy to read and easy to fix.

8
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:30.520
Reach the star with 3 blocks or fewer. The arrows move 1 square.

9
00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:34.940
Repeat 4: right, up. Just 3 blocks!

10
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:38.320
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

11
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.650
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
